Table of all nightly AMPS tests.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Format:
Name=<APP>       @@(machines): name of the test;                       required
Family=<FAMILY-ID>           : test family on the nightly report page; required
                               (ids are defined in utility/nightly/families.json)
Time=<APPRUNTIME>            : approximate runtime on supercomputer;   required
Tier=<nightly|long>          : nightly (default): Makefile.test, run every
                               night; long: Makefile.test.long, run only by
                               the periodic long routine of utility/nightly;
                                                                       optional
Ranks=<N>                    : fixed MPI rank count of a Tier=long test,
                               launched as $(TESTMPILAUNCH) $(TEST<APP>RANKS);
                               required for Tier=long, an error otherwise
Keys=<APPKEYS>   @@(machines): keys specific for <APP>;                optional
Outs=<APPOUTFILE>@@(machines): output files for <APP>, space-separated;optional
Compile=
>>>target content
>>>target content@@(machines): non-generic compile target;             optional
Rundir=
>>>target content
>>>target content@@(machines): non-generic rundir target;              optional
Run=
>>>target content
>>>target content@@(machines): non-generic run target;                 optional
Check=
>>>target content
>>>target content@@(machines): non-generic check target;               optional
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Machines can be defined:
 absent              - the same for all machines
 0+`hostname -s`+... - only for machines listed
  -`hostname -s`-... - except for machines listed.
NOTE:
Specifications (0+MACHINE_1) and (-MACHINE_2) don't contradict each other,
parameters on MACHINE_1 will be affected by both
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If Keys is absent or empty, no keys are used.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If Outs is absent or empty, file naming test_<APP> is used.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If Compile|Rundir|Run|Check is absent or empty, the default target is used 
(see makefile.test.app). 
Target is considered empty if it is no more than one line, 
i.e. ">>>" is empty (see Mars test), but ">>>\n>>>" is non-empty 
(though it is blank) and will be used for substituting the default target.

If a line starts with '>>>' is it added into the approptiate target of the Makefile.test 
started with a 'TAB'. If a line starts with '<<<' the 'TAB' is omitted.  

===============================================================================

